  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef nlp_perplexity_computation(token_ids: list, logits: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Perplexity Computation** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef nlp_perplexity_computation(token_ids: list, logits: list) -> dict:\n    ids, logs = np.array(token_ids, dtype=np.int64), np.array(logits, dtype=np.float64)\n    mx = np.max(logs, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n    lp = logs - (mx + np.log(np.sum(np.exp(logs - mx), axis=-1, keepdims=True)))\n    nll = -np.mean(lp[np.arange(len(ids)), ids])\n    return {'nll_loss': round(float(nll), 4), 'perplexity': round(float(np.exp(nll)), 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
